From 5b6c7d8e9f0a1b2c3d4e5f60718293a4b5c6d7e8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: noname <noname@example.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 11:30:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] 0033 hold the enter the clock answers with, so the host reads it

The clock 0032 arms answers the pop-up, and the pop-up stays up. Measured over
the two fresh r0.60 sessions of this boot (play-dstny6.log PID 17149,
play-dstny7.log PID 22016, board weston@192.168.1.33): the window armed the
clock at its own live marker - `wayland-video: stream window created` and
`wayland-video input: opening enter clock armed: 30000 ms then 11 more at 5s`
in the same millisecond at 11:13:43.187 - and answered 12 times 5.00-5.01 s
apart between 11:14:13.188 and 11:15:08.199, `wayland-video input: opening
enter answered (11 left)` down to `(0 left)`, beside a picture that held
`wayland-video fps=54.1 committed=8177 dropped=0 flushFailed=0` and 0 of the
DMA-BUF export class. The game did not start: the cloud session still sat at
Steam's notice 38 s later, when the player pressed Enter at the board and the
window logged `wayland-video input: key 28 vk=0xd mods=0x0 pressed=1` at
11:15:46.301 with `pressed=0` at .333 - 32 ms of key held down - and Destiny 2
went on. The two answers reach the host the same way (the window's own calls
are the calls `submitKey` makes, and the NVST codec forwards a keyboard packet
as a down and an up message with a timestamp, nothing else) and they differ in
one measured thing: the clock's press went down and came back up inside the
same microsecond, since 0032's answer calls the release right after the press,
while the finger's Enter stayed down for 32 ms. The host reads key state, so a
press that is already up when it samples is a press it never saw. 0033 makes
the answer a hold on the same clock: the press goes out on one round and the
release follows on the next round, whose interval is the hold
(OPENNOW_POPUP_ENTER_HOLD_MS, 120 ms when unset), while the follow-up answers
keep their 5 s spacing. The teardown releases a press the clock was still
holding, so a session that ended does not leave Enter down in the game.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [STM32MP25 performance work]

